+On a direct Anthropic account with **Enable prompt caching** on, Marinara marks the end of the system prompt and a chat message **Cache depth** messages back from the newest (5 by default). A change before history can invalidate the system boundary and later history. A change after the marked history boundary can keep the cached part. When the chat has a summary, a third mark goes just before **Past Events**: the turn a new summary is saved re-sends Past Events and the history, while the system prompt in front of it is still read from the cache. OpenRouter's Claude models get the same mark. Minimum cache lengths vary by model. See the provider's current [Anthropic prompt-caching guide](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching) or [OpenAI prompt-caching guide](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/prompt-caching).
 
